OAuth 1.0 (left, 8 steps)

Consumer fetches a Request Token from the Service Provider using Consumer Key + Consumer Secret + Callback URL
Service Provider issues the Request Token
Consumer redirects the user to the Provider for authorization
User grants authorization (using Request Token + Callback URL)
User is redirected back to the application
Consumer exchanges the token for an Access Token (using a Verifier)
Service Provider grants the Access Token
Consumer creates the connection

OAuth 2.0 (right, 6 steps — simpler)

Consumer redirects the user to the Provider for authorization (using Client ID + Redirect URI + optional Scope)
User grants authorization
User is redirected back to the application (with an Authorization Grant)
Consumer exchanges the Authorization Grant for an access grant
Service Provider grants access (via Redirect URI + Authorization Grant)
Consumer creates the connection

