Note: The test case will always be written in the Test tab of Postman. In the updated version, it will be Post-response script.

Validating the Status Code
Test for the response status code:
pm.test("Validate if status code is 200", () =>{
    pm.response.to.have.status(200)
});

Now let us suppose, we do not have the exact status code to be there when the request is sent but we know that the request should pass as we are sending the valid data. In that case, we can write test case which can check if status code is any one from the list.

pm.test("Validate the test is passing", () =>{
    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200,201,202,204]);
});

If we see different status codes, whether they are for passing or failing. There is some string there with the status code. For example 200 OK, 201 Created, etc. To check these strings we can write below test.

